# Concept: VK epochs

#>spw_concept_vk_epoch
#:concept =moving

^"card"{
  ~#what: "the verifying key defines an era: an epoch pins a manifest (circuit shape, content set); an upgrade is a drift-CLASSIFIED boundary, not a hot swap; game seasons literally ride VK-epochs"
  ~#why_hard: "it couples the most formal thing in the repo (circuit identity) to the most playful (seasons), and to operations (the VK ceremony runbook) — three communities, one boundary"
  ~#stitches: "settlement (a chain verifier pins a VK) ↔ dreggnet.season ↔ ops runbooks ↔ horizon's setField VALUE8 epoch entries"
  ~#trap: "treating a VK change as a deploy — it is a constitutional moment; the drift classification is what makes it survivable"
}
